
Welcome Brothers and Sisters!

New Democracy has a philosophy, Everyone In! So everyone is welcome!

I have personal views not suitable for everyone. I express many of them in this book. Let that in no way persuade anyone that New Democracy is not for them. New Democracy embraces a new kind of society: specialized morality.

Specialized morality: 1. morality is divided among people as opposed to the traditional view that morality is universal and everyone is responsible for knowing all moral rules.

In 2026 we are facing the morality of yet another new technology: AI. What is the morality of AI? If we don't use AI then does it matter?

The first rule of fight club  is that if there is a fight then you're in the fight.*

*No. No it's not. That is not the first rule of Fight Club. :-)

The first rule of specialized morality is no violence, no harm. The second rule of specialized morality is to separate opposing parties.

For example, I'm not just an atheist, I'm also an anti-theist. Anti-theists should be kept separate from theists.

So rest assured, everyone is welcome! Welcome Brothers and Sisters!

New Democracy relies on a specific type of empathy so as to achieve everyone in: thinking empathy.

thinking empathy, noun: 1. an intellectual commitment to the well being of everyone that has no limits.

Empathy is commonly thought of as putting oneself in someone else's shoes. Empath is emotionally identifying with someone else's pain. The Golden Rule is based on this definition of empathy.

There is a modernized Golden Rule, the Platinum Rule.

platinum rule, noun: 1. Treat others as the want to be treated.

I do not like this rule. First off, gold and platinum are rich people comparisons. I prefer the Information Rule.

information rule, noun: 1. Treat people as they are not as you are and this requires information. 

If we know nothing about a person the information rule degenerates to the golden rule in principle but in practice the information rule degenerates to stereotypes. These stereotypes are typically negative. limiting and harmful. In other words, stereotypes could be generalized versions of the information rule. However, most stereotypes in use in 2026 are no factual but instead are dominant culture oppressing sub-cultures.

You are my brother or sister because I practice thinking empathy. Thinking empathy includes everyone in existence. This means Trump and Hitler, or whoever the worse person possible is to you is included in New Democracy. 

Trump obviously has mental health issues. Promoting his well being means he should never be put in a position that makes that mental health worse. Trump having power over anyone, even his own kids, would not serve his well being. Trump should never be responsible for anyone, let alone the leader of any country.


How specialized is specialized morality in New Democracy? New Democracy is has two primary components: mesh nodes and projects connect mesh nodes making a mesh. Projects can span from two mesh nodes to all mesh nodes. Mesh nodes are required to be exactly thirty people. Given a population of nine billion people then there would be three-hundred million mesh nodes. Each mesh node can potentially be specialized morality.

New Democracy takes a divide and combine approach to problems. The divide is specialized morality each mesh node adopts for itself. The combine is project contracts where terms of the contract combine different moralities for common objectives.





